WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.667
-Our first guest tonight is
a Golden Globe-winning actress

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.667
you know from shows like
"Felicity" and "The Americans."

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.934
She stars in "Antlers,"
which is in theaters now.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.734
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.801
-He's not dead.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:15.167
-Yeah, he is, Lucas.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:18.367
My brother, Paul --

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:22.667
he found him in your house.

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:24.067
-No.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.100
That was my old dad,

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.801
when he was sick and mean.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.901
My new dad's related,

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:35.667
but Aiden doesn't understand,
and he needs me.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:39.100
I just have to feed him,
and he'll love me.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.367
-Please welcome back to the show
Keri Russell!

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:45.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.467
-Hi!
-Hello! Welcome back!

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.834
It's so good
to see you in person.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.234
-I know.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:06.534
-I like a horror movie where
a scene takes place by fireside.

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:08.601
-It's very similar
to how you parent, right?

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.868
You're like, "Give me food, and
then you'll stay alive."

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.167
-Yep. I also --
Every hard conversation

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.067
I have with my kids, I'm like,
"You sit on the couch.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.501
I'll start a fire.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:20.400
One side of my face
will be very ghostly lit."

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.000
-It always works better
that way, always.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.567
-This film
takes place in Oregon,

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.767
and it is sort of
a ravished community --

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:29.567
a ravaged community,
I should say.

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:31.467
-I think I'm ravishing.
-You're ravishing.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:32.701
-Ravishing.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:37.501
-You're a ravishing woman
in a ravaged community.

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:39.701
But it's got
a supernatural element.

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.767
It's a scary film.
Have you seen it in the theater?

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.167
That's one of the exciting
things about people

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:45.300
being to be to get in theaters
again is scary movies.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.133
-It is, and I'm really glad
they held it,

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:50.167
because, you know, we actually
made this three years ago,

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:53.234
or about that,
and then, as we all know,

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.601
the world stopped working
for a moment.

00:01:55.601 --> 00:01:59.033
And so they saved it, and then
we could see it in theaters,

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.701
which, by the way, you know,
this definitely should be

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:04.334
seen in theaters, and it's so
beautiful and haunting.

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:08.033
But, yes, I have these girl pals

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.701
that my kids
call "Moms Gone Wild."

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:12.100
-Your kids call you
"Moms Gone Wild"?

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.200
Wow.
-Correct.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.367
-These mom friends of mine.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.868
And we took --
The Moms Gone Wild friends

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:19.734
took our teenagers to go see
this movie last Saturday,

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.901
and it was scarier
than I thought.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:23.968
-The movie -- That's good.

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.400
-I hadn't seen it
in three years,

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.200
and I was like, "Ooh!

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.234
This is -- Whoa! This is -- Wow!

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:30.501
This a lot scarier
than I thought."

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.734
And I kept looking over
at the teenagers,

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.067
and they were like, "It's fine."

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.133
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:35.501
-So the Moms Gone Wild
were scared,

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:36.734
but the teenagers were fine.

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.567
-Moms Gone Wild -- You know,

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.601
when you see a scary movie,

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:40.767
they always show
scary-movie trailers.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:41.934
-Yep.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:44.400
-So, there was
a "Scream" trailer at first,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.567
and there's this
very scary teaser to it.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:52.133
And the two of us verbally
screamed and bonked our heads.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.234
We went "Aah!" and screamed
and bonked our heads,

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.734
and the teenagers looked at
us like, "Hey."

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.767
Like, "Get out of here."

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.467
-Your kids are so spread out --
14, 9, and 5.

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:01.901
-9 and 5, yep.

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:05.300
-So, what is Halloween like when
you have kids that are, like,

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.634
so different in
the eras of life there?

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.801
-I'm so glad I survived.
-Yeah.

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:11.968
-It's exhausting.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.367
Does anyone else
have exhausting Halloweens?

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:14.534
-Yeah.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.501
-I mean, I know it's fun,
and I grew up with a mom

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:19.467
who loved Halloween and,
like, is so into all of that.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:20.801
It's exhausting.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:21.934
You know, the teenagers are out.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.334
You're trying to make sure
they're safe.

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:24.567
The 9-year-old, you're like,

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:25.667
"Got to get them
with their friends,

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:26.934
make sure no one
gets kidnapped."

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.567
I mean, it's,
like, people everywhere --

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.167
-And did you -- Did she get
kidnapped or did you make it?

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:31.167
-Not this year.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:32.634
-Okay. Congrats.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.567
-And then the 5-year-old
is Darth Vader,

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:35.734
and he's, like, running around.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:39.234
It was craziness.
I'm so tired from Halloween.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.601
-I -- We are trying to --

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:43.234
You know, 'cause 5 is our
oldest, and 5 is your youngest.

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:44.934
So, we're trying to,
like, teach him that, like,

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:48.467
eating the candy
isn't actually part of this.

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:49.467
-Oh, no.

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.767
-Yeah, you leave
the candy on offer

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.968
for the Halloween Santa.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.400
-You know what?

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.667
That's so funny, because that's
kind of what Matthew does.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:58.801
-Yeah.

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:00.767
-And, actually,
he went out last night,

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:03.000
and I had all
three kids home alone.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.467
And Matthew was
getting ready to go,

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.834
and I was like,
"You guys, if you are good,

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:11.267
if you are good, I will let you
guys have a piece of candy

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:12.501
after dinner."

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:13.701
And they were like, "Whoo!"

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.367
And I was like, "Keep it down!
Keep it down!

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:17.634
If Matt hears, he's going to be
really bummed."

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:19.934
So, he left,
and they were like, "Candy!"

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:21.801
-Yeah. It's not fair
what they do us with the candy.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:22.901
-It's not fair.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:25.133
It's really not fair,
but it's amazing.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.801
-Your husband,
Matthew Rhys, who --

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:27.934
You guys met on "The Americans."

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.334
-It's true.

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:32.000
-And he -- A lot of people did
stuff during the pandemic.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.300
Was this a -- He bought a boat.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.634
-On eBay.
-On eBay.

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:38.501
-Yeah.

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:42.033
-Which is, like --
I would imagine most boaters

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.334
would say that's not
the place to buy it.

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.367
-I'd say that's not
the place to buy a boat.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:46.901
-And he had to do
a lot of work on it.

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:49.300
-Especially for someone
who had never had a boat before.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.434
-Okay.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:51.734
-He was like,
"Oh, this is a good idea."

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:54.667
Like, probably
after two glasses of wine

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:55.767
on the couch late at night.

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:58.234
-Yeah. The weird thing
is that he --

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.400
I mean, 'cause, again, like,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.701
it's not like eBay is like,

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:02.000
"Hey, you want to look
at a boat?"

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.133
Like, you have to go on eBay
and, like, enter "boat."

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:04.667
-Oh, he deep-dived it.
-Yeah.

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.033
-He deep-dived it, yeah.

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:08.634
-And he bought a boat
and he had to do a ton of work.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:11.400
Like, this is him,
like, doing work on his boat.

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:13.934
But, like, there was
an article in

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:15.067
"The New York Times" about this.

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:17.267
-There was.
-This is a successful boat.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:19.234
It's the same kind of boat that
Ernest Hemingway had, correct?

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:21.567
-Correct. There's only four left
in the world of that class.

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:23.434
-Wow. And here it is.

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:25.701
Look at the job
he did on this boat.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:28.300
-I know. It's really good.
Him and his captain, Kelli.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:33.634
And the thing that sold it
was that the name

00:05:33.634 --> 00:05:35.267
actually on the boat.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:36.868
Its given name was Rarebit.

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:39.267
-Oh, it pre-existed.
-It pre-existed.

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:41.901
You don't -- It's very bad luck
to change the name of a boat.

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:42.934
-Really?

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:44.634
-And when he heard
it was Rarebit,

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:48.400
there's this food thing
called Welsh rarebit.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.901
And he was like,
"I have to have this boat."

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.234
-Yeah, because he's a Welshman.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:53.901
-He's proud Welshman.
-And I was like, "Good luck."

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:55.200
-Now, has he won you over?

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.200
Because this now seems like
a lovely way to, like,

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.334
go around --

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:58.334
-It is a lovely way.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:05:59.467
And it's beautiful.

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:02.534
It's this beautiful antique
wooden thing

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:04.334
that we want to do
"Day Drinking" with you.

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:06.601
-Yeah, I would love to go
day-drinking on the sea.

00:06:06.601 --> 00:06:07.934
-Yes, right?

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:11.000
-Yeah, 'cause that's where --
The only thing that --

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.467
When I've gone day-drinking,
the only thing

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:16.000
I've wished was also happening
was just being slowly jostled.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.868
Just a light, slow jostling.

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:22.400
-A lot of our dreams
can come true together.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.501
-Well, I'm going
to hold you guys to this.

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:26.234
-You will.
-It is always great to see you.

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:28.000
Congratulations so much
on the film.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.033
You guys, that's Keri Russell.

00:06:30.033 --> 00:06:31.133
"Antlers" is in theaters now.

